('What does the expression "red tape" mean?', 'Slow official rules and paperwork', ['A police barrier at a crime scene', 'A warning sign on a road', 'Money paid as a bribe'], 'Red tape is the excessive rules, forms and procedures of officialdom that slow things down.'),
('What does the expression "back to the drawing board" mean?', 'To start planning again after a failure', ['To return to school', 'To draw a map of an area', 'To go back to an old job'], 'When a plan fails and must be worked out again from the beginning, people say it is back to the drawing board.'),
('What does the expression "to keep someone at arm\'s length" mean?', 'To avoid getting close to them', ['To shake hands with them', 'To protect them from harm', 'To watch them very closely'], "To keep someone at arm's length is to stay distant and avoid a close or friendly relationship with them."),
('What does the expression "in the same boat" mean?', 'In the same difficult situation', ['Travelling together by water', 'Working for the same employer', 'From the same family or town'], 'People in the same boat face the same problem or hardship together.'),
