('"The officer was disciplined for being ___, openly rude to a senior officer." Which word fills the gap?', 'insolent', ['innocent', 'insolvent', 'indignant'], 'Insolent means rude and disrespectful to someone in authority. Insolvent means unable to pay debts, and indignant means angry at unfair treatment.'),
